# ============================================================
#  Crises: queued by resources hitting zero (see core/rules.grim)
#  and by debt. These are the "game over" gates — each gives the
#  player one way out, at a price, before ending the run.
# ============================================================

@event crisis_collapse
title: Collapse
class: crisis
tone: grim
trigger: queued
priority: 90
art: cross
tags: crisis
scene: A narrow infirmary bed under a high arched window, a healer's lamp floating beside it.
text: The world tilts. When it rights itself you are in the infirmary, and Sister Amaranth is looking at you over her spectacles. "You have been running your body like a borrowed broom," she says.
> left: Pay for the full cure (30 gold)
  gold -large
  health +huge
  say: Three foul tonics and two days' sleep later, you feel almost human.
> right: Ask to rest instead
  if collapses >= 1:
    end ending_sent_home
  else:
    health +huge
    study -large
    mood -small
    collapses += 1
    lose sick
    say: A long, dull fortnight in bed. Sister Amaranth warns you: "Next time, I write to your family."

@event crisis_despair
title: The Grey
class: crisis
tone: grim
trigger: queued
priority: 90
art: rain
tags: crisis
# Mood at zero (rules.grim: mood on_zero). Feedback 2026-10-16: the card says so, and reaching out is no longer a free
# cure: it brings Mood back only after a breakdown that costs something else (one of four, at random).
scene: A student sitting on the edge of a dormitory bed, rain on the window, a packed trunk by the door.
text: Your spirits have hit bottom. Everything has gone grey: food tastes of nothing, lectures are noise, and you have packed your trunk twice this week and unpacked it once. It would be so easy to take the next barge and simply stop.
> left: Reach out to someone
  hint: Spirits come back, after a night that breaks something else.
  if bonds(friend) + bonds(close) + bonds(partner) > 0 or met(maud) or despairs < 1:
    chance even:
      chance even:
        study -small
        mood -tiny
        say: First you cry, properly, the way you haven't since you were small, until the window goes pale. Then you sleep straight through the morning's lectures, and wake ashamed of it.
      else:
        mana -large
        say: You walk out to the empty practice field and cast until there is nothing left to cast: fire, wind, light, anything. You come back hollow and shaking, and lighter.
    else:
      chance even:
        health -small
        renown -small
        say: You walk the grounds in the rain all night without a cloak, round and round the lawns. A prefect finds you at dawn, soaked to the skin, and the story is round the dormitory by breakfast.
      else:
        gold -medium
        mood -tiny
        say: You throw your inkwell at the wall, then the chair, then the little mirror. Afterwards you sit among the pieces, oddly calm. Replacing it all costs a small fortune.
    if bonds(friend) + bonds(close) + bonds(partner) > 0:
      mood +huge
      health +small
      say: In the morning you knock on a friend's door. They don't ask questions. They just make tea, and stay.
    elif met(maud):
      mood +huge
      health +small
      rel maud +small
      say: Old Maud finds you in the gardens and puts a trowel in your hand. "Dig," she says. You dig. It helps more than it should.
    else:
      mood +huge
      health +small
      despairs += 1
      say: Afterwards you talk to the night porter, of all people. He tells you about his own first year. It's enough, for now.
  else:
    end ending_quiet_departure
> right: Take the next barge
  hint: Spirits back for now; a second time, you go.
  if despairs >= 1:
    end ending_quiet_departure
  else:
    mood +large
    despairs += 1
    say: You get as far as the landing. The barge is late. By the time it arrives, you have decided to stay one more month.

@event crisis_probation
title: The Disciplinary Board
class: crisis
tone: grim
trigger: queued
priority: 90
art: scales
tags: crisis
scene: Three professors behind a high bench in a dim chamber, the headmistress in the centre, hands folded.
text: Two terms of failing marks. You are summoned before the Disciplinary Board: three professors and the headmistress, who looks at you with an expression of deep, patient disappointment. {flag(board_reprieve): They have seen you here before.|}
> left: Plead your case
  if flag(board_reprieve):
    end ending_expelled
  else:
    challenge negotiate journeyman likely:
      win:
        flag board_reprieve
        study +large
        gain probation
        say: You speak honestly and well. They grant you one reprieve, and a study plan that fills every evening. "There will not be a second," says the headmistress, pleasantly.
      lose:
        end ending_expelled
> right: Promise to work harder
  if flag(board_reprieve):
    end ending_expelled
  else:
    flag board_reprieve
    study +large
    gain probation
    mood -medium
    say: "Promises are cheap," says Professor Thorne. "We'll take this one. Only this one." A reprieve, a study plan in his own hand, and a very long term ahead.

# The first missed payment (M22): a reminder, with interest.
@event grisk_reminder
title: A Friendly Reminder
class: incident
tone: tense
trigger: queued
priority: 70
art: letter
tags: money
chain: debt
scene: A small, very neat note pinned to a dormitory door with a brass tack, the handwriting tiny and precise.
text: A note on your door, in a tidy goblin hand: "A payment was missed. Mister Grisk is a patient businessman. Mister Grisk charges interest on his patience." Underneath, smaller: "Pay something, or another month will be added."
> left: Scrape together what you can
  if gold > 0:
    gold = 0
    debt_missed = 0
    mood -small
    say: You empty your purse into an envelope and slide it under his door. It isn't twelve crowns. It is, says the note in reply, "a gesture. Noted."
  else:
    debt_paid -= 1
    mood -small
    say: There is nothing to put in the envelope. You write "next month, I promise" on a scrap and slide that under his door instead. The reply is a single line, "Promises are added to the ledger," and another month is.
> right: Put it out of your mind
  debt_paid -= 1
  mood -tiny
  say: You put the note in a drawer. Another month goes on the ledger, and next month the knock on your door will be louder.

@event grisk_collectors
title: Grisk's Collectors
class: crisis
tone: grim
trigger: queued
priority: 80
art: chain
tags: crisis money
chain: debt
scene: Two large trolls in ill-fitting waistcoats looming in a dormitory doorway, one holding a ledger.
text: Two trolls in waistcoats are waiting outside your dormitory. "Mister Grisk," says the larger one, "is disappointed." The smaller one cracks his knuckles, which sounds like a rockslide.
> left: Hand over everything you have
  gold = 0
  debt_missed = 0
  mood -medium
  if debt_paid >= 3:
    lose in_debt
    say: They count your purse twice and declare the debt settled. "Pleasure," says the large one, meaning it.
  else:
    debt_paid += 1
    renown -small
    say: They take every coin and your good boots, in front of half the corridor. "Partial," they say, and leave.
> right: Run
  challenge feat apprentice+ wild:
    win:
      debt_missed = 1
      mood -tiny
      say: You escape across the rooftops. They'll be back, but not this month.
    lose:
      health -huge
      debt_missed = 0
      say: You do not escape. The trolls are surprisingly gentle about breaking only one rib.
      gain injured
